<td id="A3.T5.6.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T5.6.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.23</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation on decomposition steps.</span> We study how the number of decomposition steps impacts the performance of context-guided sequential editing and provide the results in Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table A6 ‣ Appendix C More Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Towards Robust Sequential Decomposition for Complex Image Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A6</span></a>. We observe that more decomposition steps yield performance gains. Specifically, <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math> performs the best on independent chains, while <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=5</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the highest performance on editing tasks with inter-step dependencies.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A6</span>: </span><span id="A3.T6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation on decomposition steps (K) for Context-Guided Sequential Editing with <math id="A3.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{ctx}=2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{ctx}=2.5</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
<div id="A3.T6.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:496.9pt;height:62.2pt;vertical-align:-26.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(99.9pt,-12.5pt) scale(1.67307206558046,1.67307206558046) ;">
<table id="A3.T6.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T6.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T6.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><math id="A3.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A3.T6.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Single-Turn (1)</th>
<th id="A3.T6.6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">2</th>
<th id="A3.T6.6.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">3</th>
